cay, impeding its practical application. In addressing these challenges, a surface modification technique involving lithium borate (LBO) is employed through a dry coating method. The LBO-coated LRLO exhibits a uniform surface layer with a thickness of 15 nm. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAdvanced Energy Materials: Vol 14, No 46 (https://advanced.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/toc/16146840/2024/14/46)\nciteturn8search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.9 years ago; Crawled: last month; Understanding Boron Chemistry as the Surface Modification and Electrolyte Additive for Co-Free Lithium-Rich Layered Oxide\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUnderstanding Boron Chemistry as the Surface Modification and Electrolyte Additive for Co-free Lithium-Rich Layered Oxide | Request PDF (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/379014722_Understanding_Boron_Chemistry_as_the_Surface_Modification_and_Electrolyte_Additive_for_Co-free_Lithium-Rich_Layered_Oxide)\nciteturn8search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # Understanding Boron Chemistry as the Surface Modification and Electrolyte Additive for Co-free Lithium-Rich Layered Oxide ...   * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nORCID (https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0297-4522)\nciteturn8search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; #### Understanding Boron Chemistry as the Surface Modification and Electrolyte Additive for Co‐Free Lithium‐Rich Layered Oxide\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUnderstanding Boron Chemistry as the Surface Modification and Electrolyte Additive for Co‐Free Lithium‐Rich Layered Oxide - Park - 2024 - Advanced Energy Materials - Wiley Online Library (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/aenm.202401968?af=R)\nciteturn8search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.1 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; LBO coating materials are introduced as 1) it protects the surface lattice oxygen of LRLO, reducing the exacerbated generation of H_{2}O and free protons at high voltage; 2) it also reacts with PF_{6}^{−} to form thermodynamically stable BF_{4}^{−}, mitigating the generation of HF acid in the electrolyte. ... These findings have the potential to guide the design of surface modification layers for high-voltage cathode materials and inform the utilization of boron-based electrolyte additives in future applications.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUnderstanding Boron Chemistry as ... preview & related info | Mendeley (https://www.mendeley.com/catalogue/d5f26000-7e16-3cae-8e7f-3be7ba2dccae/)\nciteturn8search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # Understanding Boron Chemistry as the Surface Modification and Electrolyte Additive for Co-Free Lithium-Rich Layered Oxide\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSearch Results | Scholarly Articles, Journals, and E-Books | EBSCOhost (https://openurl.ebsco.com/results?bquery=DE+%22LITHIUM+borate%22&link_origin=&searchDescription=LITHIUM+borate&sid=ebsco%3Aocu%3Arecord)\nciteturn8search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; ### Understanding Boron Chemistry as the Surface Modification and Electrolyte Additive for Co‐Free Lithium‐Rich Layered Oxide.\n"
